    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The `output$textbox &lt;- ...` should not be inside the observeEvent. The video &quot;Effective Reactive Programming Part 1&quot; on <a href=\"https://www.rstudio.com/resources/webinars/shiny-developer-conference/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rstudio.com/resources/webinars/shiny-developer-conference/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792390328989000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Pl7AEDOEHPhh408DNVjqP\">this page</a> goes into detail as to why.<div><br></div><div>isolate({...}) does NOT mean &quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">withholds executing the logic if the action button is 0&quot;. Instead, it means that any reactive values/expressions that are accessed inside the isolate(), should NOT be listened to for changes. So for example:</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">output$textbox &lt;- renderText({</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  input$variableNumericInput</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">})</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">output$textbox would update automatically every time input$variableNumericInput changes. If instead you do this:</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></span></div><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">output$textbox &lt;- renderText({</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  isolate(input$variableNumericInput)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">})</span></div><br></div><div>then textbox will only ever show the initial value of input$variableNumericInput; it won&#39;t change. If you want to update on button press:</div><div><br></div><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">output$textbox &lt;- renderText({</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  req(input$goButtonCustom)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  isolate({</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">    input$variableNumericInput</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  })</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">})</span></div><br></div><div>Since input$goButtonCustom appears outside of the isolate(), it will cause the textbox&#39;s renderText expression to reexecute. The req() is there to prevent the rest of the code from running if the button has not been clicked. See <a href=\"https://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/req.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/req.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792390328990000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0WtQQB0XEoo84h4uqAORw3\">the article</a> for more.</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
