     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">That works, thanks heaps!<div><br></div><div>Bobbie.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Friday, March 31, 2017 at 9:47:17 AM UTC+11, Joe Cheng [RStudio] wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">The `output$textbox &lt;- ...` should not be inside the observeEvent. The video &quot;Effective Reactive Programming Part 1&quot; on <a href=\"https://www.rstudio.com/resources/webinars/shiny-developer-conference/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rstudio.com/resources/webinars/shiny-developer-conference/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792390328997000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RSx8Br1wyKNK_JYMKYacz\">this page</a> goes into detail as to why.<div><br></div><div>isolate({...}) does NOT mean &quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">withholds executing the logic if the action button is 0&quot;. Instead, it means that any reactive values/expressions that are accessed inside the isolate(), should NOT be listened to for changes. So for example:</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">output$textbox &lt;- renderText({</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  input$variableNumericInput</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">})</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">output$textbox would update automatically every time input$variableNumericInput changes. If instead you do this:</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><br></span></div><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">output$textbox &lt;- renderText({</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  isolate(input$variableNumericInput)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">})</span></div><br></div><div>then textbox will only ever show the initial value of input$variableNumericInput; it won&#39;t change. If you want to update on button press:</div><div><br></div><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">output$textbox &lt;- renderText({</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  req(input$goButtonCustom)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  isolate({</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">    input$variableNumericInput</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">  })</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">})</span></div><br></div><div>Since input$goButtonCustom appears outside of the isolate(), it will cause the textbox&#39;s renderText expression to reexecute. The req() is there to prevent the rest of the code from running if the button has not been clicked. See <a href=\"https://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/req.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/req.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792390328997000&amp;usg=AOvVaw16To68JPZngOEARzoGU1Z2\">the article</a> for more.</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Wed, Mar 29, 2017 at 8:36 PM Bobbie Shaban &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">bobbie...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>Sorry, I know you&#39;ve probably had this question before. I have performed a search in this forum but i&#39;m not quite sure if this question has been asked, it&#39;s more likely that I&#39;m not understanding properly.</div><div><br></div><div>The isolate function basically withholds executing the logic if the action button is 0? Is that correct?. The code below is some one elses example I found while searching for a solution.</div><div>So this line of logic &quot;<font color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:12.025px;white-space:pre-wrap\">finalFib&lt;- reactive({ </font><font color=\"#0000ff\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:12.025px;white-space:pre-wrap\">1</font><font color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:transparent;font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:12.025px;white-space:pre-wrap\"> / currentFib })&quot; is executed once the action button is pressed, right?</font></div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:8.5px;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.14902);font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:12.025px;border-radius:4px;line-height:18px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><code style=\"font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;border-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">shinyServer</span><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">function</span></span><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">input</span><span style=\"color:inherit\">,</span><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\"> </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">output</span><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></span><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\"> </font><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">{</span></span><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\">\r\n  </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">currentFib</span><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\"> </font><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span></span><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\"> </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">reactive</span><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">{</span></span><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\"> </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fib</span><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">as.numeric</span><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">input</span><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">$</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">n</span><span style=\"color:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></span><font color=\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\"> </font><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">}</span><font color=\"#687687\">)\r\n</font></code><code style=\"font-size:12.025px;font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;border-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\"><font color=\"#000000\">  isolate({\r\n  if(actionButton==0)\r\n  return()</font><font color=\"#687687\">\r\n</font>  </code><code style=\"font-size:12.025px;font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Droid Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;border-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\"><font color=\"#000000\">finalFib&lt;- reactive({ </font><font color=\"#0000ff\">1</font><font color=\"#000000\"> / currentFib })\r\n  })</font></code></pre></div><div><br></div><div>In my bit of code I have a number of numeric inputs that are used in an algorithm that is executed via an action button.</div><div><br></div><div>so my code is</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">observeEvent</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$goButtonCustom</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     input$goButtonCustom<br><br>     output$textbox </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">renderText</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Some text&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     variableInput </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> input$variableNumericInput<br><br>     calcFunction</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">variableInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#end observe Event</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></font></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>My code works as expected and waits until the user presses the go button before it performs the calculation (I have more inputs than above, I was just showing one for simplicity)</div><div><br></div><div>My app prints the contents of the input boxes at the same time as the result from calcFunction prints it&#39;s results as per the example below.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;Source Sans Pro&quot;,Calibri,Candara,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px\"><div>Number of cases: 100000</div><div>Number of controls: 150000</div><div>P-value threshold: 5</div><div>Odds ratio: 1.5</div><div></div></div><h3 style=\"font-family:helvetica;font-weight:bold;line-height:1.5;color:rgb(7,7,7);font-size:12pt;background-color:rgb(214,212,212);border-radius:4px\"><div>Power estimate: &gt;30%</div></h3><br></div><div>Once the button has been pressed if the user updates the numbers in the numeric Inputs the numbers for each of the inputs i.e. cases/controls/p-value are updated automatically but the calcFunction is not.</div><div><br></div><div>How would I be able to only update the output text boxes for cases/controls/p-value etc only when the action button is pressed?</div><div><br></div><div>Does that make sense? Am I doing the wrong thing by placing the logic inside an observeEvent as opposed to observe?</div><div>would some code like this help? Which I&#39;ve tried but doesn&#39;t seem to work.</div><div><br></div><div>Do I have to wrap each renderText in a separate isolate() or can I use one for the whole lot? Will this train of thought prevent the output texts being updated automatically or am I going in the wrong direction?</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">observeEvent</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$goButtonCustom</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$goButtonCustom</span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>      isolate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          </span></font><span style=\"color:#000\">     output$textbox </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">renderText</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Some text&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>               variableInput </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> input$variableNumericInput<br><br>               calcFunction</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">variableInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></font><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">             </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#end observe event</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span></font></div></code></div><br>Thanks for your help,</div><div>Bobbie.</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/5cc115bb-e55a-427b-b1f1-c8d3b1b00db8%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/5cc115bb-e55a-427b-b1f1-c8d3b1b00db8%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792390328997000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ZdLegAHJedsUur2BaageJ\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/5cc115bb-e55a-427b-b1f1-